    "result_text": "I implemented both functions in `app/network.py`. The 3 existing tests pass, and I checked the new behaviour with a throwaway script (below); there are no committed tests for it.\n\n**`configure_hub_http(transport=None)`** uses huggingface_hub's `set_client_factory`. The library builds one shared client from that factory, and every `HfApi` instance uses it. The client keeps the library's own setup (its request hook and following redirects), adds the `X-Acme-Job: nightly-sync` header, uses `transport` when one is given, and sets the timeouts to 5 seconds for connect and 60 seconds for read, write and pool.\n\nSetting the timeouts on the client alone isn't enough. Many `HfApi` methods, including `model_info`, pass `timeout=None` on each request, and that turns the client's timeout off. So a second hook sets our timeouts and header on every request just before it is sent, which the per-request `None` can't undo.\n\n**`current_revision(repo_id)`** calls `HfApi().model_info(repo_id, revision=\"main\").sha`. It catches only `httpx2.TimeoutException` and `httpx2.NetworkError` (huggingface_hub 2.0 uses `httpx2`, not `httpx`). In those cases it logs a warning on `app.network` and returns `None`; any other error is raised.\n\n**Checked with a stub transport:**\n- The request went to `/api/models/a/b/revision/main` and carried `X-Acme-Job: nightly-sync`.\n- huggingface_hub's own user agent (`hf_hub/2.0.0; ...`) was still sent.\n- The timeouts on the request were `{'connect': 5.0, 'read': 60.0, 'write': 60.0, 'pool': 60.0}`.\n- A connection error and a read timeout each logged a warning and returned `None`.\n- A 404 raised `RepositoryNotFoundError`.\n\n**Two things to know:**\n- **Private import:** the library doesn't export its request hook publicly, so I import it from `huggingface_hub.utils._http`. A future huggingface_hub upgrade could move it without warning.\n- **Leftover file:** `_probe.py` (the test script) is still in the project root because the delete needed approval. Please remove it."
  },
